{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03PF", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a93541c57f5f27b20fb4e6689dc64999905853f8bf856a1cd834f3c41fd44870", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe recall the definition.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5422b56da8a7c6846edda92d30722f2f4276d8226b7e0ae1fa9c22b0662525d1", "unit_id": "tag:03PF:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03PF", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$U$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{\\varphi_i : U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\varphi_i$", "MATH_0004": "$U_i$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$U = \\bigcup_{i\\in I}\\varphi_i(U_i)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-etale-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d62e22eea3f9736d28266b12c992bdf5fe869a2adf211744aa2e4f2482ca96ad", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:634af3c56f6ff699d43c8b918e2cc4cd8492b26bedf8666944a44ad333b7b64a", "source_text": "An <TEXTITOPEN_0001><ACCENT_0001>tale covering<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of a scheme <MATH_0001> is a family of morphisms\nof schemes\n<MATH_0002> such that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> each <MATH_0003> is an <ACCENT_0002>tale morphism,\n<STRUCT_0003> the <MATH_0004> cover <MATH_0005>, i.e., <MATH_0006>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:02b0382c90a35170b20d97215fb76e33c3a766ca858af27d9d5aa70cd14ecbd7", "unit_id": "tag:03PG:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03PF", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-etale-fpqc}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fe16761b8ecb6a701d70c29f9964d5235dcffa619b9868259718bbc71385cdf6", "source_text": "Any <ACCENT_0001>tale covering is an fpqc covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c6e5e77bd88b4b0c93f966fb14877c31e34f49a3cddbbe4ac2c846c40baf1622", "unit_id": "tag:03PH:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03PF", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$\\{\\varphi_i : U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0002": "$V \\subset U$", "MATH_0003": "$\\varphi_i^{-1}(V) = \\bigcup_{j \\in J_i} V_{ij}$", "MATH_0004": "$V_{ij} \\subset U_i$", "MATH_0005": "$\\varphi_i$", "MATH_0006": "$V = \\bigcup_{i\\in I} \\bigcup_{j \\in J_i} \\varphi_i(V_{ij})$", "MATH_0007": "$V$", "MATH_0008": "$V$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-lemma-zariski-etale-smooth-syntomic-fppf-fpqc}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9e03cfd7f7a923bae57c7ed3979c738efabe71a8ad37b43c00bcf178e918cf70", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3149c43b814b3467cc4a7663ac41212f88b5712eb7cf624c01b49dfd21b25980", "source_text": "(See also\nTopologies,\nLemma <REF_0001>.)\nLet <MATH_0001> be an <ACCENT_0001>tale covering.\nSince an <ACCENT_0002>tale morphism is flat, and the elements of the covering should\ncover its target, the property fp (faithfully flat) is satisfied.\nTo check the property qc (quasi-compact), let <MATH_0002> be an affine\nopen, and write <MATH_0003>\nfor some affine opens <MATH_0004>. Since <MATH_0005> is open\n(as <ACCENT_0003>tale morphisms are open), we see that\n<MATH_0006>\nis an open covering of <MATH_0007>.\nFurther, since <MATH_0008> is quasi-compact, this covering has a finite\nrefinement.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:03dbcc447897dcd3bdd9790463f4631d677b96e1f2f1ff6df9bb88fb8a3af938", "unit_id": "tag:03PH:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03PF", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fc12ae3b1bdc45de033e004150d8bc9fd3b6da7bd3dead652b6c4ab807f6b694", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nSo any statement which is true for fpqc coverings\nremains true <TEXTITOPEN_0001>a fortiori<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> for <ACCENT_0001>tale coverings. For\ninstance, the <ACCENT_0002>tale site is subcanonical.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:22e7a1926d02d5f886fc01a67d95b2704c1bc01b4e8ddd25f7538f6a2c3da2d9", "unit_id": "tag:03PF:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03PF", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\etale$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$S_\\etale$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$(\\Sch/S)_{Zar}$", "MATH_0008": "$S_{Zar}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-big-small}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{topologies-section-etale}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{definition-tau-site}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{definition-tau-site}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0004": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0004": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-big-etale-site}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8e876d3a730f64054ddb37f0b4c6f50317ef755ec4fb8a32c2ce97fdfedaa81e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:42726793ba2606fbdddb68f87f62f0328d0a8c41f4e3e2e0f313865be094e4da", "source_text": "(For more details see Section <REF_0001>, or\nTopologies, Section <REF_0002>.)\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nThe <TEXTITOPEN_0001>big <ACCENT_0001>tale site over <MATH_0002><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is the site\n<MATH_0003>, see\nDefinition <REF_0003>.\nThe <TEXTITOPEN_0002>small <ACCENT_0002>tale site over <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0002> is the site <MATH_0005>, see\nDefinition <REF_0004>.\nWe define similarly the <TEXTITOPEN_0003>big<TEXTITCLOSE_0003> and <TEXTITOPEN_0004>small Zariski sites<TEXTITCLOSE_0004> on <MATH_0006>,\ndenoted <MATH_0007> and <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e63ee0a4527965e851fdff02ed313a1ed9666524cbab44a2cc31d3b32447bd2f", "unit_id": "tag:03PI:statement"}
